{"nodes": [{"id": "prompts_extract_extraction_subagent", "label": "Extraction Subagent Prompt", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "references/prompts/extract.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One paper per subagent, opus. Extract only from the supplied snapshot \u2014 no prior knowledge, no fetching. Null and negative results are extracted with the same care as positive ones."}, {"id": "prompts_extract_evidence_is_an_offset", "label": "Evidence Is an Offset, Not a Sentence You Typed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/prompts/extract.md", "source_location": "Evidence is an offset", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Transcribed text is discarded and, where it mismatches the re-slice, the claim is rejected; off-by-one offsets fail the same way an invented quote fails, so start/end are copied from source.py window headers rather than counted by hand. A number without a span is worse than a missing number."}, {"id": "prompts_extract_derived_quotes", "label": "quotes[] Is Derived, Never Written", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/prompts/extract.md", "source_location": "Output", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The extraction record's quotes array is always [] from the agent and is filled by the assembler from the spans, so no excerpt in the pipeline was ever typed by a model."}, {"id": "prompts_extract_null_vs_none_declared", "label": "null Is Not 'none declared'", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "references/prompts/extract.md", "source_location": "Field rules", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For funding and COI, null means the paper did not state it, which is materially different from the paper stating there was none; conflating the two invents a fact about 